// Title: Copy Passwd Or Shadow From TMP Path
// Sigma ID: fa4aaed5-4fe0-498d-bbc0-08e3346387ba
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Joseliyo Sanchez, @Joseliyo_Jstnk
// Date: 2023-01-31 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1552.001
// Description: Detects when the file "passwd" or "shadow" is copied from tmp path
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://blogs.blackberry.com/
//   - https://twitter.com/Joseliyo_Jstnk/status/1620131033474822144
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_cp_passwd_or_shadow_tmp.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/cp" and ProcessCommandLine contains "/tmp/" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "passwd" or ProcessCommandLine contains "shadow")
